sylz (syc), PJA and PPA (Yade Bravo, MIT) are in Free Pascal and, by rule, never linked
into zpaq-std: they ship as plugins (codecs/sylz, codecs/pja and codecs/ppa, .dll or .so).

LZ4 (Yann Collet, BSD-2-Clause) and LZAV (Aleksey Vaneev, MIT), used by `-ma:lz4`
and `-ma:lzav`, are bundled in compressors/lz4 and compressors/lzav since 2.0.0
(zpaqfranz embedded them up to 65.4, for its -m6 and -m7).

The ZPAQL decoders that travel in `-ma` blocks are zpaq-std's own, except the LZMA
decoder at the core of ZPAQLZMA and ZPAQFLZMA2, by Kaido Orav (kaitz), from zpaqf
(public domain; compressors/zpaqlzma/LICENSE).
